# Testing Discipline

- Read nearby tests before adding new ones. Match local helpers, naming, and assertions.
- Check the package's `package.json` before choosing a command; this repo uses both Jest and Vitest depending on the package.
- Test the intent of the change, not just implementation details.
- Prefer the narrowest useful workspace command first, such as `npm run test --workspace=@medplum/app`, then broaden through Turbo or root scripts only when risk justifies it.
- If a change affects user workflows, include at least one interaction-level test or smoke verification path.
- Never report "tests pass" unless you ran them. Say exactly what was run and what was skipped.
- When tests are impractical, explain the blocker and provide a concrete manual verification path.
